# Production Code Is Not for Tests

Do not change production packages so tests can reach internals more easily. Tests adapt to the product; the product does not adapt to tests.

## Do not

- Add functions, methods, or fields in non-`_test.go` files whose only purpose is testing (e.g. `setXForTest`, `resetForTest`, `TestHook`, exporting helpers “for tests”).
- Widen visibility (export symbols) only to satisfy `_test.go`.
- Add config flags or env vars used only in tests.
- Branch production logic on `testing.Testing()` or build tags meant to alter runtime for tests.

## Do instead

- Test through the real public API and documented behavior.
- Use `_test.go` in the **same package** to call unexported symbols when a white-box unit test is justified—keep that code in `_test.go` only.
- Inject dependencies via constructors or interfaces defined for **production** needs (not “test doubles only” surfaces).
- Use integration/harness tests (`*_integration_test.go`, recorder harness) when behavior spans packages.

```go
// ❌ production file
func (s *Service) InjectQueueForTest(q *Queue) { s.q = q }

// ✅ _test.go in same package
func TestService(t *testing.T) {
    s := newServiceWithQueue(fakeQueue) // helper lives in test file
}
```
